  "id": "electrophysiologic-audiometry",
  "term": "electrophysiologic audiometry",
  "definition": "Electrophysiologic audiometry is a hearing test method that records the brain’s electrical responses to sound. By averaging ongoing brain-wave activity, it makes a characteristic response pattern to the sound easier to detect; it is also called evoked response audiometry or electric response audiometry.",
